+## Measured Complete Object Sizes
+
+The laboratory fixtures in [pqc-rpki-global-evaluation] were generated with OpenSSL 3.6.2 and the existing Composite provider.
+They contain complete DER-encoded RFC 6487-profiled certificates with [RFC3779] resource extensions, CRLs, ROA CMS objects, and manifest CMS objects.
+CMS sizes include the embedded EE certificate, signed attributes, and signature.
+
+| Suite | CA cert (B) | CRL (B) | ROA CMS (B) | Manifest CMS (B) |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| RSA-2048 | 1064 | 415 | 1621 | 1743 |
+| ML-DSA-44 | 4264 | 2575 | 7016 | 7138 |
+| ML-DSA-65 | 5793 | 3464 | 9434 | 9556 |
+| ML-DSA-65 + P-256 Composite | 5927 | 3533 | 9637 | 9758 |
+
+The laboratory manifests contain two fixed fileList entries; these sizes are not field-size distributions from the observed cache.
+The global projection preserves each observed manifest's actual contents instead of substituting the laboratory fixture.
+Composite ECDSA signatures are variable length, so the measured Composite sizes describe this capture; the projection uses the maximum encoded signature size stated below.
+
+Earlier, separate certificate/CRL measurements for classical reference algorithms, ML-DSA-87, SLH-DSA, and experimental Falcon-512 are retained in [pqc-rpki-lab].
+The Falcon-512 measurements use oqs-provider 0.11.0-rc1 with liboqs 0.15.0 and an experimental OID and encoding, not a final FN-DSA PKIX profile.
+Those supplementary runs do not supply the object rows for the global repository/RRDP projections and should not be conflated with the complete-object capture above.
 
